url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23425860
abstract: >-
  Canopy is a desktop app for viewing, editing and publishing phylogenetic
  trees, modelled on R's ggtree. It reads Newick, NEXUS, phyloXML and HyPhy
  results; draws layer-based figures with comparative data, PhyloPic
  silhouettes and geologic timescales; summarizes Bayesian tree sets
  (consensus, MCC, DensiTree, rogue taxa); imports BayesTraits variable-rates
  and Fabric results; and exports publication-quality PNG, TIFF, SVG and PDF.
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - phylogenetic trees
  - tree visualization
  - comparative methods
  - Bayesian phylogenetics
  - BayesTraits
